<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:25:15 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>West Bank attacks: Opposition leader Eisenkot decries "Jewish terrorism"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-attacks-opposition-leader-eisenkot-decries-jewish-terrorism</link><description>
Israeli authorities have opened an investigation after Palestinian vehicles and properties were set on fire in three villages in the occupied West Bank. Israeli soldiers were deployed to the area following the attacks, which local residents said were carried out by Israeli settlers. Gadi Eisenkot, a rival of outgoing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu, condemned the acts on X, describing them as “Jewish terrorism”. Antonia Kerrigan reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/800f91a6-e690-11f1-94e1-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-160919-161053-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/800f91a6-e690-11f1-94e1-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-160919-161053-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">850a0628-e690-11f1-9770-d1608150d187</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:25:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel investigates West Bank fires</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-investigates-west-bank-fires</link><description>
Israeli authorities have opened an investigation after Palestinian vehicles and properties were vandalised and set on fire in four villages in the occupied West Bank, in attacks local activists say were carried out by Israeli settlers. Around eight vehicles were reportedly torched and racist slogans sprayed on walls, prompting Israeli soldiers and police to deploy to the area. The attacks come amid a surge in settler violence since the outbreak of the Gaza war in October 2023, with more than 1,100 Palestinians killed by Israeli soldiers or settlers in the West Bank since then, according to an AFP tally. They also follow recent sanctions announced by the UK and Australia against eight Israeli companies involved in settlement activity. France 24 correspondent Noga Tarnopolsky shares further details from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f8b8c1ac-e679-11f1-8017-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-140613-140959-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f8b8c1ac-e679-11f1-8017-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261122-140613-140959-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fdc5c032-e679-11f1-804f-f99043976363</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:47:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Bahrain accuses Iran of striking industrial site as tankers hit in Hormuz</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261122-bahrain-accuses-iran-of-striking-industrial-site-as-tankers-hit-in-hormuz</link><description>
Bahrain accused Iran of striking a civilian industrial site on Saturday evening, as two tankers were hit in the Strait of Hormuz. Tehran reported shooting down a US drone amid stalled efforts to end the war. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30f63712-e624-11f1-976a-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/c0934c40446967fd901759e5363f0c2bf9251a33.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30f63712-e624-11f1-976a-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/c0934c40446967fd901759e5363f0c2bf9251a33.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">31c5b4d8-e624-11f1-a020-0f3a5ebf3e34</guid><pubDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:24:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30f63712-e624-11f1-976a-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/c0934c40446967fd901759e5363f0c2bf9251a33.jpg">© STR, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Eisenkot invites Netanyahu’s party for ‘marathon’ Israeli coalition talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261121-eisenkot-invites-netanyahu-s-party-for-marathon-israeli-coalition-talks</link><description>
Israeli opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has invited caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu's right-wing Likud party for coalition talks, his centrist Yashar party said Saturday. The "marathon series of talks" starts Sunday, the party said, adding that the move reflected a commitment to form "the broadest possible government" after the October election failed to deliver an outright winner.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70936d94-e5e9-11f1-943b-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6U96RP.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70936d94-e5e9-11f1-943b-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6U96RP.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7e61ef70-e5eb-11f1-a29b-5f44caa99dc9</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:49:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/70936d94-e5e9-11f1-943b-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D6U96RP.jpg">© Ilia Yefimovich, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Endurance athlete swims in Hormuz Strait</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/endurance-athlete-swims-in-hormuz-strait</link><description>
The Strait of Hormuz remains largely blocked, with Iran attacking vessels attempting to cross it. As concerns grow over the environmental impact of the war, with toxic chemicals spreading through the air and sea, one swimmer and ocean advocate has gone a step further than issuing warnings: he plunged into the polluted and dangerous waters of the strait, calling on all sides to end the conflict.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00399db4-e5c3-11f1-8eee-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-141231-141431-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00399db4-e5c3-11f1-8eee-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-141231-141431-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">056f3d7a-e5c3-11f1-b992-b90a38c59525</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:02:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Houthis launch strikes on Saudi Arabia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/houthis-launch-strikes-on-saudi-arabia</link><description>
Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen continue to exchange strikes with the Saudi-led coalition. The coalition said it intercepted and destroyed three ballistic missiles fired towards Riyadh early on Saturday. It marks the second Houthi attack on the Saudi capital in recent days, following Saudi-led strikes on Houthi targets in Yemen. Yuka Royer has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/778980c6-e58e-11f1-b8cd-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-091902-092039-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/778980c6-e58e-11f1-b8cd-ebb478925cf0/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-091902-092039-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c72fb9e-e58e-11f1-a931-1d57297cb463</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:49:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's Houthis target Riyadh after Saudi coalition's 'special operation'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261120-yemen-s-houthis-target-riyadh-after-saudi-coalition-s-special-operation</link><description>
Yemen's Houthi rebels launched strikes on Riyadh on Saturday after Saudi-led coalition air raids on Yemen, escalating a months-long surge in cross-border attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/43dab966-e511-11f1-b7af-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/44975f13e4cedc724dc3005a9fa1d30c73841d8b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/43dab966-e511-11f1-b7af-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/44975f13e4cedc724dc3005a9fa1d30c73841d8b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">453b2db8-e511-11f1-954d-5137e52b96c5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:36:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/43dab966-e511-11f1-b7af-1bac47ab2f5d/w:1024/p:16x9/44975f13e4cedc724dc3005a9fa1d30c73841d8b.jpg">© Ansurallah media centre, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iraqi security forces deploy in Hezbollah stronghold under compromise deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261120-iraqi-security-forces-to-deploy-in-hezbollah-stronghold-under-compromise-deal</link><description>
Iraqi security forces deployed ​in the Kataib Hezbollah stronghold of Jurf al-Sakhar, state media said on Friday, under a compromise deal brokered by Shi'ite politicians. Iraq's prime minister ordered a security intervention earlier this week after accusing the Iran-backed militia of smuggling state-owned oil worth ⁠hundreds of millions of dollars.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d70c954-e4bb-11f1-9f2f-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321593824833.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d70c954-e4bb-11f1-9f2f-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321593824833.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8fd3f12-e4bc-11f1-9ec1-9748c2288644</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:37:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d70c954-e4bb-11f1-9f2f-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321593824833.jpg">© Anmar Khalil, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Skyscraper in Riyadh damaged as Saudi Arabia reports surge in new Houthi attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-skyscraper-in-riyadh-damaged-as-saudi-arabia-reports-surge-in-new-houthi-attacks</link><description>
A skyscraper in Saudi Arabia's capital Riyadh was damaged on Thursday after the Gulf country reported new attacks by Yemen's Houthis. Witnesses said the city's Public Investment Fund Tower, which showcases Saudi Arabia's economic ambitions, was "damaged across several floors, with windows blown out". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/889a1214-e3ee-11f1-801f-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6BN49E.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/889a1214-e3ee-11f1-801f-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6BN49E.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2a2cb846-e3ec-11f1-b561-cdbc4a9464ea</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:58:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/889a1214-e3ee-11f1-801f-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/000-A6BN49E.jpg">© Fayez Nureldine, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gaza: Israel launched new offensive on Nuseirat</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-israel-launched-new-offensive-on-nuseirat</link><description>
Israeli tanks have moved east of the Nuseirat refugee camp in central Gaza, with witnesses reporting heavy shelling, gunfire and airstrikes as the Israeli military says it has launched an operation in a Hamas-controlled area. Strikes killed at least three people on Wednesday, and displaced families are fleeing again, saying there is no real ceasefire. Israel and Hamas accuse each other of breaking the truce in force since October 2025, while Gadi Eisenkot tries to form a government after inconclusive elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cb17a8e-e3ec-11f1-8605-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-061552-061743-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7cb17a8e-e3ec-11f1-8605-7908c4e1a3c7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261119-061552-061743-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">820c9a0e-e3ec-11f1-98f3-2567f0c1ed5f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 07:50:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Middle East crisis poses 'largest threat' to energy security in history, warns IEA</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261119-middle-east-crisis-energy-security-iea</link><description>
The International Energy Agency said on Thursday that the Middle East crisis triggered by US and Israeli strikes on Iran in February posed the “largest threat” to energy security in history. It warned that consumers were bearing more of the costs as Iran’s blockade of the Strait of Hormuz disrupted oil shipments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfcf9412-e37f-11f1-92da-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26318617092767.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfcf9412-e37f-11f1-92da-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26318617092767.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b9d06268-e3bf-11f1-a10b-a78e24423621</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:11:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bfcf9412-e37f-11f1-92da-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26318617092767.jpg">© Amirhosein Khorgooi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli army launches ground operation in Hamas-controlled area of Gaza</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-in-hamas-controlled-area-of-gaza</link><description>
The Israeli military said it had launched an operation on Wednesday in a Hamas-controlled area of central Gaza, where an AFP journalist saw Israeli tanks position themselves east of the Nuseirat refugee camp. The rare ground operation comes after inconclusive Israeli elections, with the opposition's Gadi Eisenkot trying to form a government without caretaker prime minister Benjamin Netanyahu, who has built his brand on saying he will ensure Israel's security. FRANCE 24's Daniel Whittington reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c27f5ac4-e368-11f1-97ec-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321586490001.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c27f5ac4-e368-11f1-97ec-c5c0357b2a0c/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321586490001.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dd05d4d4-e388-11f1-b338-bba3e21069a0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:55:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Writer Etgar Keret: 'The Israel my parents dreamed of' is still possible, but not under Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261118-netanyahu-s-only-2-tickets-are-racism-or-starting-a-war-he-stopped-acting-as-a-democratic-player</link><description>
François Picard is pleased to welcome Israeli writer and filmmaker Etgar Keret, author of "The Seven Good Years". Keret argues that Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu is seeking to remain in power, at any cost, including delegitimising Arab parties and prolonging conflict. "For him, it could be a never-ending war as long as he's in power. He has no incentive to stop it," our guest warns.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc28fae4-e43e-11f1-b9f8-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-09964174.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc28fae4-e43e-11f1-b9f8-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-09964174.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9436c6a0-e388-11f1-b2a0-bb68cd9c3227</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:45:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Gazans flee shelters as Israeli army launches ground operation beyond Yellow Line</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-gazans-flee-shelters-as-israeli-army-launches-ground-operation-beyond-yellow-line</link><description>
Palestinians fled their tents and shelters in central Gaza on Wednesday after Israel launched a rare ground operation in an area it withdrew ​from under a ‌2025 ceasefire. The Israeli army said it crossed the Yellow Line separating Israeli and Hamas-controlled areas "to remove a threat posed to IDF troops operating in the Gaza Strip". 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/291a44ea-e375-11f1-8738-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-18T145851Z-876917872-RC2DQOALE3WH-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/291a44ea-e375-11f1-8738-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-18T145851Z-876917872-RC2DQOALE3WH-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">946c2080-e369-11f1-8169-7b555491c4b4</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:03:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/291a44ea-e375-11f1-8738-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-18T145851Z-876917872-RC2DQOALE3WH-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg">© Mahmoud Issa, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen: Why the Houthis may besiege Aden rather than storm it</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-yemen-why-the-houthis-may-besiege-aden-rather-than-storm-it</link><description>
Bolstered by their recent military successes, Houthi rebels this week advanced close to the southern port city of Aden, the interim capital of the internationally recognised Yemeni government. Amid territorial ambitions, regional rivalries, and divisions within government forces, the potential fall of this stronghold could permanently alter the balance of power in the country.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a907106-e35a-11f1-a33f-dbb3dc175088</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:55:41 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8be454f8-c9ee-11f1-a86a-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26286485676861.jpg">© Abdulnasser Alseddik, AP</source><dc:creator>Marc DAOU</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Loud blast rocks Riyadh as Saudi-led coalition says it intercepted Houthi missiles</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261118-middle-east-live-kuwait-bahrain-report-drone-and-missile-attacks</link><description>
A powerful explosion rattled homes in Riyadh on Wednesday, journalists and residents said, as the Saudi-led coalition fighting Yemen's Houthis said they intercepted two cruise missiles fired by the Iran-backed militia. In Gaza, the Israeli military launched a rare ground operation in a Hamas-controlled area, leading dozens of families to flee their tents and shelters. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06b7fa46-86d2-11f1-8e4f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26198630293275.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06b7fa46-86d2-11f1-8e4f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26198630293275.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b1668ed4-e2f4-11f1-bc21-b5a4f32090d0</guid><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:06:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06b7fa46-86d2-11f1-8e4f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26198630293275.jpg">© Osamah Abdulrahman, AP file photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli parliament elects Eisenkot ally Matan Kahana as speaker in blow for Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261117-%F0%9F%94%B4-israeli-parliament-elects-eisenkot-ally-matan-kahana-as-speaker</link><description>
The Israeli parliament on Tuesday elected as new speaker an ally of Gadi Eisenkot, the party leader currently working to form the next government and replace current Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Matan Kahana, a former special forces soldier, is expected as soon as Wednesday to start the process of undoing much of the agenda of Netanyahu.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/855e62f8-e290-11f1-bec3-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321467242182.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/855e62f8-e290-11f1-bec3-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321467242182.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">06a31598-e2cd-11f1-95a7-ef5f71c47c23</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:24:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/855e62f8-e290-11f1-bec3-6d75ed565170/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26321467242182.jpg">© Ohad Zwigenberg, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Major setbacks for Netanyahu ahead of vote to name new Knesset speaker</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/major-setbacks-for-netanyahu-ahead-of-vote-to-name-new-knesset-speaker</link><description>
Since suffering heavy losses in Israel’s Oct. 27 election, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's party has repeatedly claimed the vote was “stolen” by Arab-led parties, possibly with foreign assistance. Those claims appear to be crumbling as he tries to cling to power, as the Israeli parliament is set to select a new speaker opposed to him. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e0651c4-e2c8-11f1-a84f-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261117-213508-213905-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e0651c4-e2c8-11f1-a84f-ff16da94d1fe/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261117-213508-213905-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">63d70684-e2c8-11f1-9b2a-e9eb4a134bed</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:05:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Did the US use ‘blackout bombs’ in Iran? Images reveal mysterious fibres at infrastructure sites</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261117-iran-us-graphite-blackout-bombs-infrastructure</link><description>
Photographs published by Iranian local media suggest that US forces may have used graphite bombs, also known as ‘blackout bombs’, against infrastructure in Iran in recent days. These weapons are designed to disrupt electricity supplies by causing short circuits rather than physically destroying power facilities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0ac6122-e286-11f1-9631-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-2026-11-17-13-57-17.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0ac6122-e286-11f1-9631-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-2026-11-17-13-57-17.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">abbdb91a-e288-11f1-9ecb-bbc38acb6f61</guid><pubDate>Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:39:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0ac6122-e286-11f1-9631-1ba7ddfab527/w:1024/p:16x9/photo-2026-11-17-13-57-17.jpg">© Iran Didehban</source><dc:creator>The FRANCE 24 Observers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Breaking taboos: Egypt's sexual revolution takes to social media</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261116-breaking-taboos-egypt-s-sexual-revolution-takes-to-social-media</link><description>
In Egypt, a sexual revolution is quietly unfolding on social media. Accounts followed by tens of thousands of people, with posts attracting millions of views, are tackling a wide range of issues surrounding sexuality – from the widespread practice of female genital mutilation (which 93 per cent of women in rural areas have undergone) to sex education and sexual pleasure.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1e52f70-df7e-11f1-ba40-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-F24-FOCUS-EGYPT-SEXUALITY-NO-MIX-Video-Mixdown-4-FF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a1e52f70-df7e-11f1-ba40-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-PKG-F24-FOCUS-EGYPT-SEXUALITY-NO-MIX-Video-Mixdown-4-FF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2f0ea93a-df7f-11f1-8f29-756da825505b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 09:50:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Mathilde DELVIGNE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Eisenkot says Netanyahu ‘cannot remain’ after alleged election interference by aide</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261116-eisenkot-netanyahu-cannot-stay-in-office</link><description>
Israeli prime ministerial hopeful Gadi Eisenkot said on Sunday caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu must leave office immediately following reports of alleged electoral interference by a Netanyahu aide. The former army chief called Netanyahu and his entourage an "immediate threat to democracy", hours after representatives discussed forming a national unity government.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">615a1e8c-e16f-11f1-b66f-d18c20ac47cd</guid><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:47:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg">© Ohad Zwigenberg, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's Houthis advance on Aden as government forces retreat to defend their capital</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-yemen-houthis-advance-to-within-60-kilometres-of-aden-military-sources-say</link><description>
Houthi forces in Yemen have advanced to within 60 kilometres of Aden, the seat of the country's internationally recognised government, military and government sources said Sunday. The embattled government earlier announced it was pulling back its last forces from the Bab el-Mandeb Strait to defend its temporary capital on the southern coast of Yemen. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92e0513c-e12a-11f1-8ab7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T135302Z-1473180222-RC26OOADAAUR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-DETAINEES.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92e0513c-e12a-11f1-8ab7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T135302Z-1473180222-RC26OOADAAUR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-DETAINEES.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f89ab374-e129-11f1-810f-b5965fbe9753</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:28:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/92e0513c-e12a-11f1-8ab7-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T135302Z-1473180222-RC26OOADAAUR-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-DETAINEES.jpg">© Khaled Abdullah, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel kills senior member of Hamas's military wing in Gaza strike</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-israel-kills-senior-member-of-hamas-s-military-wing-in-gaza-strike</link><description>
The Israeli military said on Sunday its forces had killed a senior member of Hamas's military wing in Gaza. The militant group confirmed the death of Samir Abu Younis, the commander of its Rafah brigade, adding that he played a prominent role in planning the October 7, 2023 attacks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8bd9500-e110-11f1-96bd-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T084533Z-1916440832-RC27OOA15A2T-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-HAMAS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8bd9500-e110-11f1-96bd-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T084533Z-1916440832-RC27OOA15A2T-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-HAMAS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5d92877e-e112-11f1-80af-bf3cc1bef008</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:41:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8bd9500-e110-11f1-96bd-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-15T084533Z-1916440832-RC27OOA15A2T-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-HAMAS.jpg">© Haseeb Alwazeer, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran claims drone attack on US military base in Bahrain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-claims-drone-attack-on-us-military-base-in-bahrain</link><description>
Bahrain issued two alerts of potential threats on Sunday, its first such warnings since September as blasts rocked the capital, Manama. It comes after Iran targeted an airbase in the US-allied island state, ending a long lull in strikes during the Middle East War and comes as negotiations to end the conflict remain at a stalemate, with the US maintaining its naval blockade and Iran its stranglehold over the strait of Hormuz. Story by Rachael Griffiths.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc1d38c8-e108-11f1-8b7b-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-160212-160405-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dc1d38c8-e108-11f1-8b7b-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-160212-160405-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e170475c-e108-11f1-ab96-f165ee9aaa0a</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:29:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Bahrain says air defences destroyed several Iranian drones attacking US base</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/bahrain-says-air-defences-destroyed-several-iranian-drones-attacking-us-base</link><description>
Bahrain issued two alerts of potential threats on Sunday, its first such warnings since September. The second Iranian drone attack in three days, ending a long lull in strikes during the Middle East war. Diplomatic efforts to end the almost nine-month conflict have yet to produce a breakthrough, with ​sporadic attacks continuing. Details from the ground by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Tehran, Reza Sayah.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84b2607c-e0f9-11f1-b274-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-130317-130744-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84b2607c-e0f9-11f1-b274-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-130317-130744-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89cee620-e0f9-11f1-b619-d9dce5f4b66f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:55:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Global diesel prices ease as winter approaches</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/global-diesel-prices-ease-as-winter-approaches</link><description>
Global diesel prices, which have remained elevated since the start of the Iran war and the blockade of the Strait of Hormuz, have fallen sharply in recent weeks as Gulf exports recover and global oil supplies get back on track for the first time since February. The price drop is being felt in Europe, where prices remain roughly 77% above pre-war levels, and in the US, where the national average fell below $6 a gallon on Saturday. Details by Liza Kaminov.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2255b7f8-e0e0-11f1-a02e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-100412-100553-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2255b7f8-e0e0-11f1-a02e-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261115-100412-100553-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">281836fc-e0e0-11f1-ad3e-9f4696c62486</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:40:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran claims drone attack on US military airbase in Bahrain</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-iran-claims-attack-on-us-military-airbase-in-bahrain</link><description>
Iranian military confirmed on Sunday an attack on a US military base in Bahrain, in its second targeting the Middle Eastern country in the space of three days. Bahrain's military said it had intercepted several Iranian attacks, with the foreign ministry confirming its air defence systems had shot down Iranian drones, preventing them from reaching their intended targets.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3bb0cb5a-e0d8-11f1-a866-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/000-99GY7E6-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3bb0cb5a-e0d8-11f1-a866-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/000-99GY7E6-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a80550d4-e0d6-11f1-997f-8119674c1597</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:57:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3bb0cb5a-e0d8-11f1-a866-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/000-99GY7E6-1.jpg">© 2026 Planet Labs PBC, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Three sentenced to death over Jordan church attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261115-three-sentenced-to-death-over-jordan-church-attack</link><description>
A Jordanian court on Sunday sentenced the three gunmen responsible for a terror attack on a church funeral procession in the village of Hamoud that killed nine and wounded others. The attack prompted retaliatory strikes on "terrorist organisations" in neighbouring Syria. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb10e528-e0d1-11f1-ba89-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299487770405.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb10e528-e0d1-11f1-ba89-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299487770405.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">41467eaa-e0d0-11f1-ab7a-d9b8b6b92b26</guid><pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:53:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eb10e528-e0d1-11f1-ba89-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299487770405.jpg">© Raad Adayleh, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu renews call for Israeli unity government as Eisenkot dismisses 'tricks'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261114-netanyahu-renews-call-for-israeli-government-unity-as-eisenkot-dismisses-tricks</link><description>
Israeli caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Saturday renewed his call for a national unity government with Gadi Eisenkot, who dismissed the appeal as a political ploy. This comes as the incoming premier is in the midst of negotiations to form a new administration.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9d87c1e-e06a-11f1-b45a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/eb428c66bf6978a929203d6ac1afd3964fb560b1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9d87c1e-e06a-11f1-b45a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/eb428c66bf6978a929203d6ac1afd3964fb560b1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eac268f6-e06a-11f1-afd8-addf77e06d09</guid><pubDate>Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:35:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9d87c1e-e06a-11f1-b45a-f71d22e7fea9/w:1024/p:16x9/eb428c66bf6978a929203d6ac1afd3964fb560b1.jpg">© Ilia Yefimovich, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Turkey and Qatar pledge unified stance against attacks in mutual defence pact</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261113-turkey-and-qatar-pledge-unified-stance-against-attacks-in-mutual-defence-pact</link><description>
Turkey and Qatar signed a mutual defence agreement Friday, pledging a unified response to any attack on either country, the two leaders said in a joint statement. The defence pact follows the Mecca Joint Defence Agreement signed by Turkey, Pakistan and Saudi Arabia in August.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e18af32-df9b-11f1-903b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T145055Z-1247391648-RC22NOA8HWLE-RTRMADP-3-TURKEY-QATAR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e18af32-df9b-11f1-903b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T145055Z-1247391648-RC22NOA8HWLE-RTRMADP-3-TURKEY-QATAR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2bd949e-df99-11f1-bdcc-23840e8dab80</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:06:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e18af32-df9b-11f1-903b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-13T145055Z-1247391648-RC22NOA8HWLE-RTRMADP-3-TURKEY-QATAR.jpg">© Murat Cetinmuhurdar, Turkish Presidential Press Office via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
